node_modules
dist
.vite

# public/circuit is deliberately NOT ignored. It holds the 1.8 MB of proving
# artifacts the browser needs, refreshed by `npm run sync:circuit`.
#
# They are committed because a deploy builds on a machine with no circom, and
# because the verifying key is pinned on chain: a regenerated zkey differing by
# a byte would change vk_hash and every unlock would be rejected. build.sh
# skips the MPC contribution and CI re-derives the hash, so they stay
# reproducible despite being checked in.
